    "input": "search_document: Based on the handbook excerpts provided, here is the information regarding the refundability of your gift cards:\n\n**Refund Timeframe for Unused Cards**\nUnused gift cards can be refunded to the original payment method within **30 days** of the purchase date [returns].\n\n**Applicability to Bulk/Corporate Orders**\nThe handbook excerpts **do not specify** whether this 30-day refund policy applies differently to bulk or corporate orders. The policy states that \"Unused gift cards can be refunded... within 30 days of the purchase date\" without distinguishing between individual and bulk purchases [returns]. Additionally, the purchase limits section notes that there is \"no limit to the number of gift cards you can buy in a single day,\" provided each card meets the minimum value requirement, but it does not mention special terms for bulk orders [gift_cards].\n\n**Important Conditions for Refunds**\n*   The refund is only available if the gift cards are **unused**. Once a gift card has been partially used, the remaining balance cannot be refunded to cash or credit [returns].\n*   If the cards were purchased with a credit card, the refund will be processed to that same credit card. If purchased with other methods (e.g., PayPal or debit), the refund will be issued as store credit [returns].\n*   Please allow **5 to 7 business days** for the refund to appear in your account [returns].\n\n**Recommendation**\nSince the handbook does not explicitly confirm if bulk orders are exempt from or subject to different terms than the standard 30-day policy, and given your concern about cash flow, I recommend escalating this ticket to a human agent to verify if any special corporate terms apply to your specific volume of purchases.\n\n[returns]\n[gift_cards]",
